'''Big Town''' (Japanese: '''ミレニアムタウン''' ''Millennium Town'') is an {{pkmn|animated series}}-exclusive town in [[Johto]] introduced in ''[[PK07|Pikachu & Pichu]]''. It has since also been featured in several shorts including ''[[Pichu Bros. in Party Panic]]'', ''[[HS06|Of Meowth]] [[HS07|and Pokémon]]'', ''[[Trouble in Big Town]]'', and ''[[HS09|Big Meowth,]] [[HS10|Little Dreams]]'', and it is also the only location visited in [[Pichu Bros. mini]].

[[File:Pokémon Clubhouse.png|thumb|left|220px|The Pokémon Clubhouse]]
The town is known for being the home of the [[Pichu Brothers]], who constantly make mischief along with their posse of friends {{p|Smoochum}}, {{p|Magby}}, {{p|Wooper}}, and {{p|Teddiursa}}. The Pokémon Clubhouse, a large playground constructed entirely of disused items, is their hangout spot.

A {{p|Lapras}} ferry, taxis, and double decker buses can be found here for transportation.

{{MTR}} returned to Big Town from a week-long vacation away from [[Jessie]] and [[James]] in ''Of Meowth and Pokémon''. He soon decided that he wanted to construct a giant statue dedicated to himself, however the plan never eventuated. Instead he became embroiled in the Pichu Posse's antics, and by the end of ''Big Meowth, Little Dreams'', it was time for him to return to {{TRT}}.

There are many apartment buildings around here as well as a skyscraper. Notable monuments include {{p|Magikarp}} and {{p|Tauros}} statues and a fountain.
